1
00:00:00,479 --> 00:00:02,840
of coccidiosis.

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:07,479
Wimper heard nothing of this affair and the eggs were duly delivered, a grocer's

3
00:00:07,479 --> 00:00:12,479
van driving up to the farm once a week to take them away.

4
00:00:12,479 --> 00:00:16,720
All this while, no more had been seen of Snowball.

5
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:23,840
He was rumored to be hiding on one of the neighboring farms, either Foxwood or Pinchfield.

6
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:30,279
Napoleon was by this time on slightly better terms with the other farmers than before.

7
00:00:30,279 --> 00:00:34,600
It happened that there was in the yard a pile of timber which had been stacked

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,520
there 10 years earlier when a beech spinney was cleared.

9
00:00:39,520 --> 00:00:44,359
It was well seasoned and Wimper had advised Napoleon to sell it.

10
00:00:44,359 --> 00:00:49,439
Both Mr. Pilkington and Mr. Frederick were anxious to buy it.

11
00:00:49,439 --> 00:00:54,960
Napoleon was hesitating between the two, unable to make up his mind.

12
00:00:54,960 --> 00:00:59,000
It was noticed that whenever he seemed on the point of coming to an agreement

13
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,279
with Frederick, Snowball was declared to be in hiding at Foxwood, while when he

14
00:01:05,279 --> 00:01:10,560
inclined towards Pilkington, Snowball was said to be at Pinchfield.

15
00:01:10,560 --> 00:01:15,199
Suddenly, early in the spring, an alarming thing was discovered.

16
00:01:15,199 --> 00:01:19,560
Snowball was secretly frequenting the farm by night.

17
00:01:19,560 --> 00:01:23,960
The animals were so disturbed that they could hardly sleep in their stalls.

18
00:01:23,960 --> 00:01:29,000
Every night, it was said, he came creeping in under cover of darkness and

19
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,439
performed all kinds of mischief.

20
00:01:32,439 --> 00:01:34,159
He stole the corn.

21
00:01:34,159 --> 00:01:38,119
He upset the milk pails. He broke the eggs.

22
00:01:38,119 --> 00:01:40,520
He trampled the seedbeds.

23
00:01:40,520 --> 00:01:43,920
He gnawed the bark off the fruit trees.

24
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:49,880
Whenever anything went wrong, it became usual to attribute it to Snowball.

25
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:55,520
If a window was broken or a drain was blocked up, someone was certain to say

26
00:01:55,520 --> 00:01:58,760
that Snowball had come in the night and done it.

27
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:03,399
And when the key of the store shed was lost, the whole farm was convinced that

28
00:02:03,399 --> 00:02:07,000
Snowball had thrown it down the well.

29
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,199
Curiously enough, they went on believing this even after the mislaid key was

30
00:02:12,199 --> 00:02:15,439
found under a sack of meal.

31
00:02:15,439 --> 00:02:20,199
The cows declared unanimously that Snowball crept into their stalls and

32
00:02:20,199 --> 00:02:22,560
milked them in their sleep.

33
00:02:22,560 --> 00:02:29,279
The rats, which had been troublesome that winter, were also said to be in league with Snowball.

34
00:02:29,279 --> 00:02:35,279
Napoleon decreed that there should be a full investigation into Snowball's activities.

35
00:02:35,279 --> 00:02:39,920
With his dogs in attendance, he set out and made a careful tour of inspection of

36
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:46,079
the farm buildings. The other animals following at a respectful distance.

37
00:02:46,079 --> 00:02:52,960
At every few steps, Napoleon stopped and snuffed the ground for traces of Snowball's footsteps,

38
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:57,000
which, he said, he could detect by the smell.

39
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:04,439
He snuffed in every corner, in the barn, in the cowshed, in the hen houses,

40
00:03:04,439 --> 00:03:07,000
in the vegetable garden, and found traces of Snowball almost
